+# CONTRACT — Real-Time Collaborative Document Editor
+
+## Structural
+- [ ] `createApp(dbPath?)` exported from `src/server.ts` → returns `{ app, start(port?), stop() }`
+- [ ] `start(0)` listens on a random port and returns the actual port number
+- [ ] `stop()` closes HTTP server, all WebSocket connections, and the DB
+- [ ] `npm run build` compiles cleanly
+- [ ] `npm run lint` passes
+
+## REST API
+- [ ] `POST /documents {title, content?}` → 201 with `{id,title,content,version,createdAt,updatedAt}` → test
+- [ ] `POST /documents` without title → 400 → test
+- [ ] `GET /documents` → 200 array of docs → test
+- [ ] `GET /documents/:id` → 200 doc; unknown id → 404 → test
+- [ ] `PUT /documents/:id {title?,content?}` → 200 updated doc, version bumped; unknown → 404 → test
+- [ ] `DELETE /documents/:id` → 204; unknown → 404 → test
+- [ ] `GET /documents/:id/history` → 200 array of operations (version history) → test
+
+## WebSocket
+- [ ] Connect to `/ws/:docId` → receives `{type:'sync', content, version}` → test
+- [ ] Connect to unknown docId → receives `{type:'error'}` and closes → test
+- [ ] Send `{type:'op', op:{type:'insert',position,content}, baseVersion}` → applied + broadcast `{type:'op', ops, version}` to all clients → test
+- [ ] Delete op `{type:'delete',position,length}` applied + broadcast → test
+- [ ] Malformed op (bad position / missing fields / unknown type) → `{type:'error'}`, server does not crash → test
+
+## Conflict resolution (OT)
+- [ ] Two concurrent inserts at same baseVersion both preserved (nothing dropped) → test
+- [ ] insert transformed against prior insert/delete → test ot.ts directly
+- [ ] delete transformed against prior insert (split when insert inside range) → test
+- [ ] delete transformed against prior delete (overlap removed) → test
+- [ ] 10 concurrent clients each sending many ops → final server content contains all inserted chars, no corruption → test
+
+## Persistence
+- [ ] Data survives `stop()` + new `createApp(samePath)` — document + ops present → test
